    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA striking architect designed contemporary Mews, enjoying generous well-presented accommodation, superbly located off Dartmouth Road tucked away in this premier location off Upper Leeson Street within a few minutes' walk of St. Stephen's Green and Dublin City Centre. \n\nNo. 47 is a most appealing Mews which has recently been remodelled and refurbished to include a new kitchen, flooring and bathrooms. There are many interesting design features including the sunken living room, gallery landing with feature steel balustrade. The accommodation extends to an impressive approx. 189sqm. / 2,034sq.ft. (to include the attic) briefly comprises: reception hall, off which there is a guest wc., utility & L shaped room ideal for fully self-contained home office. Off the inner hall, there is a stepped down living, with double sided solid fuel Boru stove, window seat and door out to the front courtyard. The dining area leads through to a impressive kitchen with breakfast room off with bow window and arch through to sun room. Upstairs on the first floor, there are three generous bedrooms, a shower room and a staircase that leads to the attic, which is converted and comprises a large attic room with bathroom. The rear garden has a sunny westerly aspect with low maintenance astroturf.\n\nThe location is second to none within a short stroll to Ranelagh village with its choice selection of highly regarded restaurants, pubs and specialist shops. The popularity of this location cannot be overstated you can walk into St. Stephen's Green in under ten minutes and enjoy all the benefits the city has to offer. The Luas is also easily accessible providing access to some of Dublin's most sought after schools as well as Dundrum Town Centre and beyond."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 1.35m x 3.20m\nwith sky light, marble tiled floor and door to\n\nGuest W.C. / Utility - \nwith whb, wc, plumbing for washing machine and gas fired central heating boiler.\n\nStudy - 5.40m x 4.35m\n(maximum measurement) of L-shaped room with extensive fitted shelving, study and computer area, fitted press, tiled floors, cloaks hanging area and double sliding doors leading to front and courtyard areas.\n\nInner Hall - 1.75m x 7.35m\nwith tiled floor, recessed down lighting and glazed windows looking down into\n\nLiving Room - 4.30m x 3.90m\nwith pine timber floor, double sided solid fuel Boru stove, fitted storage unit, window seat and door out to courtyard.\n\nDining Area - 3.85m x 3.55m\nwith tiled floor, recessed down lighting and double sided stove off which there is a feature curved partition wall which separates the\n\nKitchen - 3.15m x 3.90m\nrecently fitted by Michael Farrell Kitchens with a range of press and drawer units, stone worktops from Miller Bros, one and a half bowl stainless steel sink unit, four ring hob with extractor over, integrated siemens appliances including dishwasher, oven, microwave/oven, space for American style fried/freezer, recessed down lighting and tiled floor.\n\nBreakfast Room - 3.15m x 3.55m\n(average measurement) into bow window, with tiled floor and arch to\n\nSun Room - 2.50m x 2.60m\nwith pine timber ceiling and glazed folding doors opening out to a low maintenance rear garden.\n\nUPSTAIRS - \nGallery landing with feature steel balustrade\n\nLanding - 3.00m x 5.00m\nwith shelved hotpress, pine timber flooring, fitted shelving and storage units.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.30m x 3.40m\nwith glazed door and sliderobe wardrobes\n\nShower Room - \nLuxurious Spa inspired with vanity whb, wc, rain maker shower, tiled walls and floors, heated towel rail.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.90m x 2.45m\nwith pine timber flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.15m x 3.95m\nwith pine timber flooring and bay window\n\nStaircase - \nwith steel bannister railings leading up to\n\nAttic Room - 4.35m x 5.35m\nwith fitted storage, five Velux roof lights, landing with Velux roof light, under eaves storage press and pine timber flooring.\n\nShower Room - \nwith wc, vanity whb, heated towel rail, shower, tiled walls and floors, recessed down lighting and Velux roof light.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
